WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.083
Commit a business fact. The booking owner establishes that the booking is confirmed, then reliably publishes the associated fact. Publication and storage must have an explicit failure strategy.

2
00:00:14.083 --> 00:00:25.833
Fan out independently. The event channel makes the fact available to separate subscribers. Each subscriber has a distinct business responsibility and its own processing state.

3
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:37.750
One subscriber lags. Analytics becomes slow while receipt processing continues. Subscriber delay is observable; it should not silently redefine the original booking outcome.

4
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:49.750
Deliver the event twice. A repeated delivery uses the same logical event identity. Consumers must avoid awarding points or producing another external effect accidentally.

5
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:59.917
Evolve the contract. Add compatible fields carefully and test old consumers. Retained events and delayed subscribers may outlive the latest deployment.

6
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:12.833
Plan recovery and replay. Replay analytics when appropriate, but do not resend historical receipts automatically. Reprocessing policy depends on the side effects owned by each subscriber.
